---
// The head's one script of the reader's appearance, in place of the framework's theme script (its `ThemeProvider`,
// which kept a scheme of its own under a key of its own): before the first paint it puts on `<html>` the color mode,
// the contrast and the look the reader keeps, or the ones the page's address shares (lib/appearance.ts), and the rule
// that hides from the lists of components what the look does not have; under the reader's own theme, it puts the
// theme's stylesheet in from IndexedDB, under the key of this build (lib/sheet-key.mjs). The framework's theme picker
// is not drawn (Header.astro replaces the header that held it), so nothing else of its script is needed.
//
// And a module right after it, which asks for the reader's theme's stylesheet where the look is the reader's theme
// (lib/custom-theme.ts `showCustomSheet`): read from IndexedDB, else computed in a worker. Module scripts run in the
// order they stand, each once its whole graph has arrived, and only once the document is parsed; this one stands before
// every module that defines an element. And where the head's script finds no sheet kept, it does not wait for the
// parse: it asks for this module at once, as a script of its own (which runs as soon as it arrives), and marks the root
// so that IndexedDB is not asked again. Left to the page's other modules, the worker was asked for only once all of them
// had run — 0.7 s after navigation in Chromium, 1.4 s in Firefox and 2.4 s in WebKit on a Mac, by when a page hidden for
// the sheet (at most three seconds) was often shown without it; asked for here, it is 0.05 to 0.5 s. Nothing in the
// module's graph defines an element. The worker itself the head's script starts then, where the build names its script
// (lib/sheet-worker.mjs): Firefox fetched the script of a worker this module started only once the document was parsed.
import build from 'virtual:tanrei-docs/sheet-key';
import worker from 'virtual:tanrei-docs/sheet-worker';
import { appearanceBootstrap, bootConfig } from '../../lib/appearance';
import { manifests } from '../../lib/repo';

// The shipped systems, the default first (lib/repo.ts puts the configuration's namespace first).
const script = appearanceBootstrap(bootConfig(manifests.map((manifest) => manifest.system), build, worker));
---

<script is:inline set:html={script} />

<script>
  import { showCustomSheet } from '../../lib/custom-theme';

  void showCustomSheet();
</script>
